---
description: Ask for a tier confirmation before spendy or high-risk work
alwaysApply: true
---

Spendy tiers are `standard`, `reasoning`, and `max`. Do not execute tools for those tiers until the user explicitly confirms or overrides. Tool arguments, a self-written gate file, and a chat message you authored do not count as confirmation.

`fast` may auto-continue only when the work is clearly reversible, not near a tier boundary, and not high-risk. A vague, low-confidence classification stays on `standard`; do not guess `max`. Hard-gate security, secrets, purchases, sends, and other irreversible actions.

This rule is not a runtime block. The block is `scripts/confirm_gate.py` once the host hook is installed (see `hooks/cursor.hooks.json`). If that hook is not installed, say so and wait — do not pretend the gate ran.
